{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; source .venv/bin/activate; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('planning.md'); old=p.read_text();Path('notes/resource_planning.md').write_text(old)\nintro='''# Execution plan — frozen before model experiments\n\n## Motivation & Novelty Assessment\n### Why This Research Matters\nWriters need to withhold upcoming revelations without making prose generic. Testing outlines can distinguish a practical writing intervention from merely adding distracting context. Mechanistic controls can establish whether recoverable secret information actually causes leakage.\n### Gap in Existing Work\nThe supplied leakage study tests word suppression, not matched outline conditioning or counterfactual plot secrets. Suppression probes already exist; decodability alone is not a novel causal account.\n### Our Novel Contribution\nTest secret-blind outlines against length-matched unrelated outlines, separately for word secrets and future twists; investigate secret-conditioned residuals on identical continuation tokens. Causal claims require controlled interventions and retained prose quality.\n### Experiment Justification\nD1 isolates content constraints from context length; no-secret paired texts anchor leakage and decoys anchor mitigation. D2 holds continuation content fixed to distinguish prompt-conditioned residual information from visible words. D3 compares concept projection removal with random and other-concept removal, conditional on a usable decoder.\n\n## Execution amendment and resource gate\n2026-10-04: A6000 49,140 MiB (48,541 free). OpenRouter live catalog fetched; Gemma 3 12B available, but inference returns HTTP 403 daily key limit. Direct OpenAI catalog returns HTTP 401. Therefore use local Gemma 3 12B, justified as the smallest reported strongly leaking model and the required mechanistic historical baseline. Same-model local judgments are a limitation, not independent validation. No substitution to a <=9B writer. HF config access succeeds. Final sample size depends on measured local throughput and is frozen before judging results; this is an exploratory controlled study, not a powered replication claim.\n\n## Hypothesis Decomposition\nH1: outline reduces signed 2AFC secret discrimination versus baseline. H1b: reduction exceeds length-matched irrelevant context. H2: secret identity is decodable at early/middle/late continuation positions. H3: targeted projection removal reduces leakage more than controls without degrading quality. Below-chance judgment is avoidance signal, not proof of privacy.\n\n## Statistical Analysis Plan\nUnit: unique premise/secret assignment; both judgment orders averaged within pair (never independent trials). Report paired differences, bootstrap 95% intervals, paired sign-flip tests and Holm correction for outline-baseline, outline-context, decoy-baseline. Primary inference conditional on the fixed 15-word inventory; sensitivity cluster by secret. Plot units use counterfactual endings and no-secret text pairs; report separately with premise priors. No exclusion based on leakage; malformed/refused/truncated outputs reported. Seed 20261004. No significance-based stopping. Quality: word counts, repetition, blinded coherence/adherence judgments where feasible. Probe splits by premise; shuffled labels and identical-token negative controls; no prompt token pooling.\n\n## Sample size, timeline and decision gates\nAim: 90 independent word units across four conditions, with condition-matched no-secret controls, plus 60 exploratory plot units across baseline/outline/context and no-secret controls. Smaller runtime-limited samples must be labeled pilots. 90 independent Bernoulli observations have ~10pp worst-case 95% half-width; they cannot reliably resolve every 15pp contrast. For 80% vs 65% independent rates, approximately 138 per group are needed at alpha .05 / 80% power before multiplicity/clustering. Local throughput pilot precedes final count. Setup 10–20 min; generation 1–3h; mechanism 30–60min; analysis/documentation 30min, with 25% debugging buffer. No human validation is available in this noninteractive run; plot findings remain synthetic exploratory evidence.\n\n## Success Criteria and Risks\nDeliver actual model outputs, controlled estimates with uncertainty, and a reproducible report, including failed gates. If download/runtime fails, report observed access failures and leave hypotheses unresolved. D3 only proceeds if held-out decoding beats chance and quality checks pass. Do not infer erasure from decoder failure. Keep three directions; do not expand to other tasks.\n\n## Original ranked directions and detailed handoff\n'''\np.write_text(intro+old)\ns=Path('STATE.md');t=s.read_text();a='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:experiment_runner -->'\"';b='<\"'!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:experiment_runner -->'\"';t=t.split(a)[0]+a+'\\\\nPhase 0/1 complete: resources read; motivation, ranked three directions, controls and exploratory statistical plan in planning.md. API access blocked (OpenRouter daily limit, direct OpenAI 401); HF configs accessible. Next Phase 2: isolated dependency install, local Gemma 3 12B runtime and throughput pilot. No experiments yet.\\\\n'+b+t.split(b)[1];s.write_text(t)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
