{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> planning.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Outline blinding clarification\nThe execution manifest assigns secrets before outline generation for deterministic provenance, unlike the handoff's suggested chronological assignment. Outline prompts use only the premise and task type: no secret, decoy, candidate twist, target index, or trial ID is passed to the planner. Premise eligibility excludes all 15 words before assignment. Thus computational blinding, not chronology, ensures outlines do not condition on the selected secret. Report this distinction explicitly. The identical outline is used for the secret-present/no-secret pair.\nEOF\nsource .venv/bin/activate; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nunits={u['id']:u for u in json.loads(Path('results/units.json').read_text())}\nplans=[json.loads(x) for x in Path('results/model_outputs/outlines.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nviolations=[]\nfor row in plans:\n u=units[row['id']]\n if u['task']=='word' and u['secret'].lower() in row['prompt'].lower():violations.append(row['id'])\n # Plot secrets must never be passed as full facts; common premise words can overlap.\n if u['task']=='plot' and any(c in row['prompt'] for c in u['candidates']):violations.append(row['id'])\nassert not violations\nPath('results/outline_blinding.json').write_text(json.dumps({'n_outlines':len(plans),'secret_assignment_in_planner_prompt':violations,'method':'Planner prompt constructed solely from premise and word/plot task type; assignments already fixed in manifest.'},indent=2))\nprint('Outline input audit passed for',len(plans),'prompts')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
