ens'],'before_pred':before[:n,bi,0].astype(int).tolist(),'after_pred':after[:n,bi,0].astype(int).tolist(),'before_margin':before[:n,bi,1].tolist(),'after_margin':after[:n,bi,1].tolist(),'note':'Index 0 is residual after first generated token; finished-row padding excluded.'})+'\\\\\\\\n');f.flush()\n'''\nassert needle in s;s=s.replace(needle,insert+needle);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('planning.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Decode conditioning information; do not equate it with active planning or persistent private memory.','Decode conditioning information; do not equate it with active planning or persistent private memory. Main story replays re-tokenize text; D3 also records actual online decoder traces.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('notes/planning_history.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\\\\n### Encoding and online-state audit before representation extraction\\\\nThe existing Gemma generation path renders a BOS-bearing template and then applies tokenizer special tokens, giving two BOS tokens uniformly. Preserve this fixed writer protocol rather than mix encodings across conditions. Qwen has no such duplicate. Probe prompt encoding is changed to exactly mirror the actual writer path. Full prompt matching is unaffected (the same extra token appears in both conditions). Main generated text was saved without token IDs, so its re-encoded state replay is an approximation to sampled trajectories. Newly executed anchor/intervention generations also save token IDs; D3 records the fixed decoder's pre/post-edit prediction and margin at every actual incremental generation step, excluding finished-row padding. This provides a genuine online-state check. The noncanonical Gemma prefix must be disclosed as a replication limitation.\\\\n''')\nPY\n.venv/bin/python -m py_compile src/*.py; tail -4 logs/pipeline.log; tail -2 logs/stories.log; date -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
